WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.169
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Beto O'Rourke.

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:06.706
You mentioned, and I don't
want to just pass over it

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:10.110
without talking about exactly
how awful it is.

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:13.646
But Governor Abbott made it --
Basically the state of Texas

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:16.916
investigating parents who
provide gender-affirming care

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:18.651
to their children,
basically investigating them

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:20.653
for child abuse.
You went on Mother's Day

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:24.490
and you made dinner for
one of these families.

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:25.824
-I did.

00:00:25.824 --> 00:00:28.627
-Played a little music,
as I know you like to do.

00:00:28.627 --> 00:00:33.699
And can you just tell us, you
know -- and I'm sorry that

00:00:33.699 --> 00:00:36.069
so much of this is so
depressing, but can you tell us,

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:37.637
what is it like for a family
like that,

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:40.406
to be basically
almost criminalized

00:00:40.406 --> 00:00:42.374
for being a loving parent?

00:00:42.374 --> 00:00:45.378
-First thing I'll tell you is,
I've met families like

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:48.914
the Briggles all over the state
of Texas,

00:00:48.914 --> 00:00:51.517
and these parents are
the most loving parents

00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:52.751
you'll find anywhere.

00:00:52.751 --> 00:00:56.555
They're doing their best to help
their kid navigate

00:00:56.555 --> 00:00:59.392
this incredibly difficult time
in their lives,

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:01.627
and they're searching
for answers,

00:01:01.627 --> 00:01:02.895
just loving the hell
out of them,

00:01:02.895 --> 00:01:04.530
just trying to make sure that
they're okay.

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:06.165
And our governor, Greg Abbott,

00:01:06.165 --> 00:01:09.002
is proposing charging them
with child abuse.

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:10.670
And if that charge is sustained,

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:12.872
not only taking their trans kid
from them,

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:14.873
but every other child
in the household,

00:01:14.873 --> 00:01:17.677
placing them in a foster-care
system in Texas

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:19.512
that is the worst-run
in the country,

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:23.450
where 100 kids in that system
died last year in the custody

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:25.351
and the care of
the state of Texas.

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:27.519
Instead of fixing that system
and the vulnerable kids

00:01:27.519 --> 00:01:29.689
that are in it, he's going to
take these kids

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:31.490
from their loving parents
and put them there.

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:35.194
So I wanted to show up on
Mother's Day, cook a great meal,

00:01:35.194 --> 00:01:38.431
bring some flowers, have a beer,
and just make sure that we

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:40.900
shined a light on
this loving family

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:44.070
so that our fellow Texans
understand what's at stake.

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:47.173
I mean, they might lose what I
take for granted

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:48.841
with Amy and our three kids,

00:01:48.841 --> 00:01:51.477
and I want to make sure that we
fight for them and fight for

00:01:51.477 --> 00:01:53.545
everybody who's under attack
in Texas right now.

00:01:53.545 --> 00:01:54.947
So showing up for them

00:01:54.947 --> 00:01:56.449
and standing up for them
was important.

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:57.550
-That's really great
that you did that.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.652
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah, happy to.

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:01.221
-Let's be honest.

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:05.058
How was the dinner you made?

00:02:05.058 --> 00:02:07.060
What do you think?
-It was great.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:11.497
The one thing I can make really
well is a diner-style hamburger

00:02:11.497 --> 00:02:15.568
where you press the beef
down into the pan.

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:18.137
Some Velveeta cheese slices.
-Okay, gotcha.

00:02:18.137 --> 00:02:22.708
-My wife, Amy, added this twist
where we use an English muffin

00:02:22.708 --> 00:02:24.077
instead of a regular bun.

00:02:24.077 --> 00:02:26.813
Mayonnaise and a raw onion
on it.

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:29.748
Just all of that together is
just amazing.

00:02:29.748 --> 00:02:32.218
-Do you use their pan?

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:33.953
Did you use their pan
or did you bring your own?

00:02:33.953 --> 00:02:36.456
-We were cooking for so many
people that we used

00:02:36.456 --> 00:02:38.791
their cast iron,
and I bought a cast iron

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:40.059
and donated it to the house
as well.

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:42.027
-Okay, that's fair. That's cool.

00:02:42.027 --> 00:02:43.663
-We didn't want to show up
empty-handed.

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:45.064
-No, that's true.
-Yeah.

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:46.166
-If you showed up at our house,

00:02:46.166 --> 00:02:47.900
my wife would not let you
near our pans.

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:50.169
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.169 --> 00:02:52.171
Hey, you know, somebody
who was talking about

00:02:52.171 --> 00:02:54.941
and then ultimately decided
against running for governor

00:02:54.941 --> 00:02:56.276
of Texas was
Matthew McConaughey,

00:02:56.276 --> 00:02:59.712
who is a friend of the show.

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:01.981
Would there be room for Matthew
to do something

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:04.283
in an O'Rourke administration,
if you won?

00:03:04.283 --> 00:03:05.651
-Absolutely.
-Yeah.

00:03:05.651 --> 00:03:06.920
-This guy's a great Texan.

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:09.255
Beyond being
an extraordinary actor,

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:12.625
when the chips are down in
our state, this guy shows up.

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:16.162
So, we had a horrific shooting
in El Paso in 2019.

00:03:16.162 --> 00:03:19.832
23 people were killed
after Greg Abbott, Donald Trump,

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:22.501
and others warned of
this invasion of Mexicans

00:03:22.501 --> 00:03:24.137
and immigrants who were
coming to get us.

00:03:24.137 --> 00:03:27.473
McConaughey showed up to
El Paso, raised money,

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:30.276
donated it to the community,
was there,

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:31.811
you know, physically present
to make sure

00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:33.613
that we all knew
that he was with us.

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:35.782
When we had this winter storm
last year

00:03:35.782 --> 00:03:38.784
and Abbott couldn't keep the
lights on, the power went off,

00:03:38.784 --> 00:03:41.788
hundreds died, tens of billions
of dollars of damage,

00:03:41.788 --> 00:03:44.257
McConaughey gets all of his
famous friends together,

00:03:44.257 --> 00:03:45.925
and they raise millions of
dollars for the state.

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:48.160
So this guy is there for Texas

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:49.661
and he's got such
an amazing heart,

00:03:49.661 --> 00:03:52.999
so whatever he wants to do
and whoever he can help,

00:03:52.999 --> 00:03:55.468
we want to turn him loose
and let him do that.

00:03:55.468 --> 00:03:57.904
But he's an example of
the spirit of the state.

00:03:57.904 --> 00:03:59.938
I don't know if the guy is
a Republican or a Democrat,

00:03:59.938 --> 00:04:01.073
and it doesn't matter

00:04:01.073 --> 00:04:03.142
because before we're either
of those things,

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:05.878
we're Texans, we're Americans,
we're human beings,

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:07.981
and we should start treating
one another that way.

00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:09.549
And so we're going to do that
in Texas.

00:04:09.549 --> 00:04:12.685
[ Cheers and applause ]
-You have often --

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:15.154
Attention has been paid to
the fact that you really --

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:18.424
you know, it's a giant state,
and you get out and you drive

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:21.160
around and you go to places
that maybe people

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:22.961
who run for governor
don't ever stop by.

00:04:22.961 --> 00:04:24.630
Is that the plan
this time again?

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:26.465
I know you were a little --
You know, during COVID,

00:04:26.465 --> 00:04:30.235
the way you organize, the way
you ran elections in the past

00:04:30.235 --> 00:04:31.704
wasn't available
in the same way.

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:33.806
Is it nice to be back out there
seeing Texans face-to-face?

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:35.842
-I love it.
I love being on the road.

00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:37.243
I love showing up in communities

00:04:37.243 --> 00:04:38.678
where they maybe don't
expect you.

00:04:38.678 --> 00:04:41.447
So you're going to expect us
in Austin and Houston, Dallas,

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:43.582
El Paso, my hometown,
San Antonio,

00:04:43.582 --> 00:04:44.951
the Rio Grande Valley.

00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:48.454
But you show up in Childress,
Shamrock, Texas, Pampa,

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:50.189
where Woody Guthrie
spent some time,

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:52.024
Dalhart, Amarillo, San Angelo.

00:04:52.024 --> 00:04:54.861
These places are so red,
you can see them glowing

00:04:54.861 --> 00:04:57.797
from outer space as you are
orbiting the planet,

00:04:57.797 --> 00:04:59.665
but they're also unrepresented

00:04:59.665 --> 00:05:02.200
because where Democrats
fear to tread,

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:04.737
Republicans don't have to
show up and contest the vote.

00:05:04.737 --> 00:05:06.972
And so folks don't have anyone
to hold accountable,

00:05:06.972 --> 00:05:10.042
anyone to share their hopes with
or their concerns.

00:05:10.042 --> 00:05:13.346
When we show up and hold
a town hall, I learn so much,

00:05:13.346 --> 00:05:18.117
but I also build support
and trust in that community,

00:05:18.117 --> 00:05:19.552
and we bring in some more votes.

00:05:19.552 --> 00:05:21.820
And at the end of the day,
I mean, we lost to Ted Cruz

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:23.689
by 2 1/2 and a half points,
right?

00:05:23.689 --> 00:05:25.525
There are millions more Texans

00:05:25.525 --> 00:05:27.360
who've since been added
to the rolls

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:28.827
and millions who've been
effectively,

00:05:28.827 --> 00:05:30.997
through voter suppression,
kept from voting.

00:05:30.997 --> 00:05:33.199
We're targeting those who've
been the targets of

00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:34.467
intimidation and suppression

00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:37.169
so that they provide
the margin of victory

00:05:37.169 --> 00:05:39.205
when we win this thing
on November 8th.

00:05:39.205 --> 00:05:40.840
So I love traveling the state.

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:42.041
It's the right way to do it.

00:05:42.041 --> 00:05:43.475
And I think it's the only way
to win.

00:05:43.475 --> 00:05:46.112
-Well, you know, stay healthy
out there.

00:05:46.112 --> 00:05:47.580
I know it probably takes a lot
out of you.

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:49.348
And thanks so much for making
time for us today.

00:05:49.348 --> 00:05:51.350
-Thank you.
I really, really appreciate it.

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:52.752
-Guys, that's Beto O'Rourke.

